What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/position
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.16.7 (local bring-up)
Description:
		Read-only decimal position most recently reported by the
		dual-hall-slider input device: 0, 1 or 2. The initial value is
		-1 until a valid, debounced measurement has been reported.

		This is the same cache exposed by EVIOCGABS for the configured
		input axis, not an instantaneous hardware read. It is updated
		while the input device has an open consumer. The board describes
		the physical direction; no audio or key policy is assigned.
		Rejected measurements retain the last reported position.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sample_valid
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.16.7 (local bring-up)
Description:
		Read-only boolean. 1 means the latest poll read both channels,
		passed the full-scale checks and classified a candidate.
		0 indicates no current sampling, a transport/range/classification
		failure, suspend, or pending resampling after calibration.

		A candidate may still be pending debounce. This attribute does
		not guarantee that the cached position represents an already
		completed physical transition.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/hall_raw
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.16.7 (local bring-up)
Description:
		Read-only pair of fresh signed decimal IIO counts, in end-0,
		end-2 order. Reads are serialized with polling and calibration.
		The value is not cached. Failed IIO transfers, magnetic full
		scale or system suspend result in a read error rather than an
		invented pair. Per-sensor IIO raw attributes can also be used
		for diagnostics and expose full-scale values.

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/calibration
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.16.7 (local bring-up)
Description:
		Root-writable selector calibration. A read returns either
		"uncalibrated" or six signed decimal counts:

		pos0_end0 pos0_end2 pos1_end0 pos1_end2 pos2_end0 pos2_end2

		Write one complete six-integer set, separated by spaces, commas,
		tabs or newlines. Values are checked against available channel
		ranges. Adjacent signed field differences must have consistent
		ordering and be separated by more than twice the configured
		hysteresis. Invalid sets are rejected without changing the
		active calibration. "reset" removes calibration.

		Applying calibration resets pending debounce and requires a
		new sample; it does not fabricate an input event. Calibration
		is volatile and has no effect on sensor registers, audio policy
		or Android persist/NV storage. Userspace can restore a saved
		set for the same physical device.
